Package: praxis-prime
Architecture: any
Depends: python3 (>= 3.12), bubblewrap
Description: local-first autonomous AI agent
 Praxis Prime is a local-first autonomous AI agent for Linux
 (alpha: M0–M3 roadmap complete; some blueprint MVP items deferred).
 The binary package installs a virtual environment at /opt/praxis-prime
 and puts praxis-prime, pprime, and praxis-primed on PATH. It bundles the
 locked runtime wheels under each project's own license.
 .
 The optional Textual TUI (extra [tui]) is not part of this package, and
 pip is not shipped. Add the extra with ensurepip, then pip:
 /opt/praxis-prime/bin/python -m ensurepip --upgrade
 /opt/praxis-prime/bin/python -m pip install 'textual>=8.2,<9'
 .
 The package installs praxis-prime.service and
 praxis-prime-workers.slice under /usr/lib/systemd/user and does not
 enable them. Stub units are not installed. The package does not enable
 linger. It Depends on bubblewrap for the sandbox.
 .
 Build it with packaging/deb/build-deb.sh. That script does not need
 debhelper or root. The built binary is architecture-specific (the host
 dpkg architecture) because cryptography and argon2-cffi include compiled
 extensions, and it Depends on the interpreter it was linked against
 (python3.12 on Ubuntu 24.04). This source stanza stays Architecture: any
 so the same script can be run on another Debian architecture.
 .
 Not published to an APT repository. The maintainer address uses the
 reserved .invalid domain and does not receive mail.
